1
00:00:00,063 --> 00:00:03,943
-I called about the apartment. You said--
-I know what I said. I know what you said.

2
00:00:04,109 --> 00:00:06,949
(Past Sheldon:)I know what my mother said
on March 5th, 1992.

3
00:00:08,363 --> 00:00:10,453
(Past Sheldon:)What is the sixth noble gas?

4
00:00:10,616 --> 00:00:12,496
(Past Leonard:)-What?
-You said you're a scientist.

5
00:00:12,659 --> 00:00:16,079
(Past Sheldon:)-What is the sixth noble gas?
-Uh, Radon?

6
00:00:17,122 --> 00:00:19,252
(Past Sheldon:)Are you asking me or telling me?

7
00:00:20,459 --> 00:00:22,089
(Past Leonard:)Telling you?

8
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:26,090
(Past Leonard:)Telling you.

9
00:00:26,256 --> 00:00:28,046
(Past Sheldon:)All right. Next question.

10
00:00:28,217 --> 00:00:29,887
(Past Sheldon:)Kirk or Picard?

11
00:00:30,469 --> 00:00:32,969
(Past Leonard:)Oh, uh-- Well, that's tricky. Um--

12
00:00:33,138 --> 00:00:37,808
Well, original series over
Next Generation, but Picard over Kirk.

13
00:00:38,477 --> 00:00:39,557
(Past Sheldon:)Correct.

14
00:00:40,938 --> 00:00:43,818
(Past Sheldon:)You've passed the first barrier
to roommatehood.

15
00:00:43,982 --> 00:00:45,442
(Past Sheldon:)You may enter.

16
00:00:46,193 --> 00:00:47,733
(Past Leonard(Enters apartment. It is bare except for two lawn chairs, a television and some whiteboards):)Oh, this is pretty nice.

17
00:00:55,827 --> 00:00:58,417
(Past Leonard(Enters apartment. It is bare except for two lawn chairs, a television and some whiteboards):)-The bedrooms are back there?
-That depends.

18
00:00:58,580 --> 00:01:02,020
(Past Leonard:)I don't understand.
Their existence is conditional?

